# Planet acquisition working files (planet_folger_search_order_download.ipynb).
#
# Everything here is REGENERABLE from the notebook and free to re-fetch, so it is
# cache, not source. Two of these are large enough to matter: previews are ~5 MB per
# scene at native resolution (139 MB for the 30 survivors, 86 MB for the 18 rejects)
# and downloads/ holds the ordered GeoTIFFs you actually paid quota for.
planet_folger/tile_previews/
planet_folger/udm2_scratch/
planet_folger/downloads/

# Gate-2 cloud rejects, split out of tile_previews/ so the folder matches the review
# queue -- browsing tile_previews/ directly used to show all 48 gate-1 scenes, including
# 82%-cloud ones the pipeline had already discarded. The JPEGs are ignored; the README
# listing the 18 scenes and their aoi_clear scores is TRACKED, because it is the reserve
# pool if a delivery fails and it costs nothing to carry.
planet_folger/rejected_cloud/*.jpg
planet_folger/rejected_cloud/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Caches. Deleting any of these just forces the work again:
#   aoi_clear.json   UDM2 gate-2 scores    (~27 min to rebuild at concurrency 8)
#   tile_ledger.json monthly tile spend    (resets on the calendar month anyway)
#   review_labels.json  your gate-3 calls  (NOT re-derivable - see note below)
planet_folger/aoi_clear.json
planet_folger/aoi_clear.tmp
planet_folger/tile_ledger.json
planet_folger/review_labels.json

# DELIBERATELY TRACKED, do not add these to the list above:
#   gate2_survivors.csv     the 30-scene review queue
#   screened_candidates.csv gate-3 results incl. panels_seen
#   manifest_*.csv          what was actually ordered; join key to the hydrophone record
#
# review_labels.json is ignored because it is per-reviewer scratch that changes on every
# click, but it is the ONE file here that cannot be regenerated by re-running anything -
# it is human judgement. screened_candidates.csv (tracked) is the durable record of it,
# so run the collect cell before you finish a session.
